From d8fe13ba12e46efbef1bc96f2ee9e1100f32c900 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:56:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] identity: unify device naming - fix the custom_clientlist
 revert/clobber defects + one name priority everywhere

Master store stays custom_clientlist (no new store). Four write-path defects
fixed and two readers unified so a rename made anywhere shows everywhere:

1. MASS REVERT: the boot normaliser pads every tuple to 9 fields, but
   del_custom_clientlist (deleteOfflineClient.cgi), the api.asp register
   add/del/list paths parsed with a strict 6-field vstrsep and silently
   DROPPED every padded entry on rewrite - removing one offline client wiped
   all custom names. Now tolerant (6..9) and non-target tuples are kept
   byte-identical.
2. RENAME APPENDED DUPLICATES: reaper set_name compared the tuple's NAME
   field against the MAC (tuple is name>MAC>...), so the old record was never
   removed; first-match readers (gk_client_name -> Devices/GK pages) kept
   showing the OLD name while last-key-wins JSON readers showed the new one =
   the field "rename doesn't propagate / reverts" reports. Now matches the
   real MAC field, drops ALL old records for the mac, and preserves the old
   record's trailing fields (group/type/icon). Boot normaliser additionally
   drops older duplicates (last wins) so existing field devices self-heal.
3. STALE-SNAPSHOT CLOBBER: the stock rename popup rebuilt the whole
   custom_clientlist from a page-load snapshot, erasing any rename made
   elsewhere since. It now re-reads the live nvram at save time (falls back
   to the snapshot on fetch error) and clears duplicate records on splice.
4. delete_client_in_group_list iterated a 4KB stack copy of a 64KB-class
   list - deletes silently no-op'd past 4KB. Now iterates a heap copy.

Readers unified: Gatekeeper (devices + pending) now resolves
custom_clientlist first with the self-reported hostname as fallback
(was inverted); DHCP Leases gains a unified Device Name column (same
get_clientlist chain as every other page) beside the raw lease hostname.

Verified: make shared + make httpd both exit 0 (no new warnings in edited
regions); client_function.js + DHCP page inline JS parse clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
